{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_us54rixs3h2jsaqiv6w7a7tjpyyugtp4r7tdwzjgw473ou75f7kq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **One real translation bug found and fixed.**\n\n## The bug (Phase C, row E2)\n\nThe Rust did `let rnd = unsafe { &mut *rnd }` before touching `rnd.state[..]`. Forming a `&mut cn_rnd_t` **requires 8-byte alignment**, so a misaligned `cn_rnd_t*` aborted the process (`misaligned pointer dereference`), while the C — plain `uint64_t` loads/stores with no alignment check — accepts it fine on x86-64.\n\nFix: `cn_rnd_next` now takes `*mut cn_rnd_t` and accesses state only via `addr_of_mut!` + `read_unaligned`/`write_unaligned`, never forming a reference. Store order (`state[0]` then `state[1]`) and one-read-per-word structure preserved, so aligned output is bit-identical.\n\n## Results\n\n| Phase | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| A | `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md` in crate root, derived by grep from the C |\n| B | 15 tests, all 14 `CONFIGS.md` rows ✓ |\n| C | 5 tests, all 5 `ERRORS.md` rows ✓ |\n| D | 3 tests — symbol diff **empty**; 1 feature combo × 2 profiles ✓ |\n\n23/23 tests pass in **debug and release**, zero warnings. Both `.so`s are loaded via `libloading`; the Rust is never called directly.\n\nTwo notes worth flagging:\n\n- **The C library has no error surface at all** — zero `if`/`assert`/`return -1`/enum/length params. `ERRORS.md` rows E4 (out-of-range enum) and E5 (bad lengths) are genuinely vacuous, so instead of faking them I wrote tests that assert the *justification* still holds against `lib.h` (they fail loudly if an enum or length param ever appears).\n- **Row E1 (null pointer) is profile-sensitive.** Debug `ub_checks` trap the null deref → SIGABRT; C faults → SIGSEGV. That's a dev diagnostic, not an ABI difference, so E1 makes its exact signal comparison against the **release** cdylib (both SIGSEGV) and separately asserts the debug `.so` still dies fatally rather than silently returning.\n\nI also mutation-tested the harness (flipped `>> 17` → `>> 18`): 14/15 Phase B tests failed in both profiles, confirming the rows aren't vacuously passing. Only C1 survived, correctly — the all-zero absorbing state is insensitive to that constant. `c_src/` is untouched apart from the `build/` dir.\n\n`bash translation/tools/check_features.sh` reruns everything; it derives features from `Cargo.toml` (currently none) rather than hard-coding, and builds the cdylib per profile since `cargo test` won't build a cdylib-only lib target."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":93603,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":443,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ba30cda-1da0-4e30-a68f-d181b526446a","uuid":"20ad25b9-01e3-464c-b43b-768a66175019","timestamp":"2026-09-03T11:21:26.058Z"}
